{"name":"Used Oil","hex":"#231712","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"used","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of use","In used to."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That is or has or have been used.","That has or have previously been owned by someone else."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/used"},{"term":"oil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Liquid fat.","Petroleum-based liquid used as fuel or lubricant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lubricate with oil.","To grease with oil for cooking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Petroleum","blocks":[{"text":"Petroleum, also known as crude oil or simply oil, is a natural resource that appears as a yellowish-black liquid chemical mixture found in geological formations, consisting primarily of hydrocarbons. The term petroleum refers to both naturally occurring unprocessed crude oil, as well as to petroleum products that consist of refined crude oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Petroleum_sample.jpg/330px-Petroleum_sample.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petroleum","wikidata":"Q22656"},{"title":"Waste oil","blocks":[{"text":"Waste oil is defined as any petroleum-based or synthetic oil that, through contamination, has become unsuitable for its original purpose due to the presence of impurities or loss of original properties."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waste_oil","wikidata":"Q262336"},{"title":"Oil","blocks":[{"text":"Oil is a liquid with varying degrees of viscosity depending on temperature. Oil is any nonpolar chemical substance that is composed primarily of hydrocarbons and is hydrophobic and lipophilic. Oils are usually flammable and surface active. Most oils are unsaturated lipids that are liquid at room temperature."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil","wikidata":"Q42962"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Oil_well.jpg/500px-Oil_well.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Oil_well.jpg/500px-Oil_well.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOil_well.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Photo_lg_kuwait.jpg/500px-Photo_lg_kuwait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Photo_lg_kuwait.jpg/500px-Photo_lg_kuwait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhoto_lg_kuwait.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png/500px-Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png/1280px-Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png/500px-Treibs%26Chlorophyll.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The close structural similarity of vanadium porphyrin compound (left) extracted from petroleum and chlorophyll a (right) established the biological origin of petroleum.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATreibs%26Chlorophyll.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Gusher_Okemah_OK_1922.jpg/500px-Gusher_Okemah_OK_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Gusher